      "relations": "A unit shift toward saving rather than withdrawing or holding no savings is associated with 0.2956 kg/m² lower BMI (SE=0.0791, 95% CI [-0.4505,-0.1407], p=1.85e-04; standardized beta=-0.0559). The hypothesis does not explicitly identify which height measurement was used to derive BMI."
    },
    {
      "text": "Greater patience on the 1989 household-savings-action proxy is associated with lower odds of obesity in 1989.",
      "context": "NLSY79 core sample (n=6,074); logistic regression defining obesity as BMI ≥30; obesity prevalence is 12.3%.",
      "variables": [
        "Was more money put into or taken out of R/spouse savings since last interview, 1989",
        "Weight of respondent, 1989"
      ],
      "relations": "A unit shift toward greater patience is associated with approximately 12% lower obesity odds (OR=0.876, 95% CI [0.815,0.942], logit coefficient=-0.132, p=3.5e-04). BMI is derived from weight and height, but the height column used is unspecified."
    },
    {
      "text": "Greater patience on the 1989 household-savings-action proxy is associated with lower subsequent BMI in 1992.",
      "context": "NLSY79 forward-looking analysis (n=5,062); household-level savings proxy, with no pregnancy indicator for the 1992 BMI wave.",
      "variables": [
        "Was more money put into or taken out of R/spouse savings since last interview, 1989",
        "Weight of respondent, 1992"
